    {
      "id": "claim_3416a3bb405b4daca32610816f38b7b0",
      "statement": "Water-loss scope must separate covered direct physical damage, reasonable emergency mitigation, source-component work, pre-existing or maintenance conditions, improvements, contents, loss-of-use issues, and other-insurance or salvage effects; valuation and payment must use the supported covered scope and the applicable form's settlement basis rather than an estimate alone. Under HO 04 90 (2026-01), Coverage A and B follow the attached policy's settlement basis, while Coverage C is actual cash value unless the Declarations state otherwise.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://forms/HO/MS/HO-04-90/2026-01.md#L49-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aff48b136b272ae7a04bf3529107f1607cc454e270064b41d8352e8365c1ea32:"
