      "id": "claim_35206be5d1744c4382f2a100c0758aba",
      "statement": "Water-loss claims must be escalated when claimed, incurred, or reasonably anticipated exposure exceeds $25,000 without waiting for final value, and also when source, duration, evidence, coverage terms, competing scope, shared responsibility, contamination, suspected fraud, representation, litigation, recovery, or unusual compromise issues require authority review; referral does not stop claim progress.",
